From e9ef3804ad4d0c05f50608a64f34fc862a556f8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:00:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: restore MCU replies before L1 beacon updates

The L1 pre-stop path disables the IRQ tasklet and all NAPI instances.
Polling MT_MCU_CMD completes the SER handshake, but it does not receive
the replies to synchronous beacon update commands. Sending those commands
before npu_post_reset therefore causes a timeout and another full reset.

Restore the saved MCU RX queues and bootstrap the IRQ tasklet before
updating beacons. Reuse the full-reset helper, including its terminal
check, and retain the existing failure path if bootstrap is refused.
Leave data NAPI and the TX worker stopped until normal post-reset restore.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 mt7996/mac.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7996/mac.c b/mt7996/mac.c
index 0067ef7..688682d 100644
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -2633,7 +2633,11 @@ void mt7996_mac_reset_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	if (err)
 		goto fail_unlock;
 
-	clear_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state);
+	/* Beacon updates wait for MCU replies, not the polled SER states. */
+	err = mt7996_mac_restart_mcu_enable(dev);
+	if (err)
+		goto fail_unlock;
+
 	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy)
 		clear_bit(MT76_RESET, &phy->mt76->state);
 
